{
  "requirement": "Carries an I/O failure or a diagnostic for invalid source input, such as an unknown language or invalid UTF-8 in a request for text.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub enum SourceError {\n    Io(std::io::Error),\n    Invalid(String),\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Debug for SourceError;\nimpl Display for SourceError;\nimpl Error for SourceError;\nimpl From<std::io::Error> for SourceError;\nimpl From<SourceError> for std::io::Error;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The text prescribes a public enum with two variants and five trait implementations. Each is a structural obligation, because a differently shaped type would break the declared API even if it behaved the same at runtime. The supplied roots cover all of them in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/public.rs`:\n- `enum[SourceError]` declares `Io(std::io::Error)` and `Invalid(String)`. It also carries `#[derive(Debug)]`, which satisfies `impl Debug for SourceError`.\n- `impl[SourceError/std::fmt::Display]` formats each variant by delegating to its inner value.\n- `impl[SourceError/std::error::Error]` provides `Error`.\n- `impl[SourceError/From<std::io::Error>]` maps an I/O error to `Self::Io`.\n- `impl[std::io::Error/From<SourceError>]` unwraps `Io` and wraps any other variant with `Self::other`.\n\nThe obligation that the type carries an I/O failure or a diagnostic for invalid input is met by the two variants. `SourceFile::text` produces `Invalid` for bad UTF-8, and `StructuralRule::compile` produces `Invalid` for an unknown language. These are producers of the value, so they need no marker. All roots are marked with {impl}, and no gap remains.\n\nbehavioral: The tests adequately cover the observable obligations of `requirements.sdk.sources.SourceError`.\n\n- **`Invalid` carries a diagnostic.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs#fn[invalid_source_errors_display_the_diagnostic]` builds `SourceError::Invalid(\"unsupported source language\")`. It uses it as `&dyn std::error::Error` and asserts that `to_string()` equals the diagnostic. This covers both `Display` and `Error`.\n- **Invalid UTF-8 produces `Invalid`.** `source_bytes_error_kinds_and_language_names_round_trip` reads the bytes `[0xff, 0xfe]` and asserts that `text()` returns `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` with a non-empty message.\n- **An unknown language produces `Invalid`.** The same test calls `search_structure` with `LanguageId` `CustomLang`. It asserts `Err(SourceError::Invalid(message))` and that the message contains `CustomLang`.\n- **`From<std::io::Error>` and the `Io` variant.** The same test converts `std::io::Error::other(\"unreadable source\")` with `SourceError::from`. It asserts the result is `SourceError::Io(_)` and that its `Display` is `unreadable source`.\n- **`From<SourceError> for std::io::Error`.** The same test converts both variants. An `Io` error keeps its message. An `Invalid` error gives an `ErrorKind::Other` error with the diagnostic as its message.\n- **`Debug`.** The tests call `unwrap()` on `Result<_, SourceError>`, which only compiles if `Debug` is implemented. The requirement states no particular `Debug` output. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` in `public_api.rs` checks that the enum is exported.\n\nThe requirement lists no other behaviour that needs a test.",
  "references": "9b29d087a4b9e7bbb5084b18eb3718473389e07f2cd9a18040dae029c47db357",
